{#-
  data-form="updates" — email updates capture.

  While features.formsOpen is false NO input, checkbox or submit button is
  rendered: only the message. That is deliberate (design-source/README.md §5) —
  a visually dimmed form is still keyboard-focusable and submittable, which
  fails WCAG. There is no endpoint, no vendor and no third-party script in
  either state; the backend wires to the data-form hook.
-#}
{% if features.formsOpen %}
<div data-updates-form>
  <form class="ft-form" data-form="updates" novalidate>
    <label class="skip-link" for="ft-email">Email address</label>
    <input id="ft-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" required>
    <button type="submit">Get updates</button>
    <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="consent" required><span>Yes &mdash; email me Uncost updates. We use your address for updates only: we won&rsquo;t sell your data or use it for partisan targeting, and you can unsubscribe anytime. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></span></label>
  </form>
  <div class="ft-note" data-updates-note role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
</div>
{% else %}
<div data-updates-form data-form="updates" class="form-off">
  <div class="form-off-msg">Sign-ups open soon.</div>
  <div class="form-off-sub">The updates list opens at launch. Nothing to enter yet.</div>
</div>
{% endif %}
